Tobias Mummert <teergrube@phreaker.net> writes:

> I'm running NetHack on a Linux box, using a famebuffer console
> with 1280x1024 resolution (160x128 chars) - no X11 environment.
> So the Nethack window is displayed in the upper left corner of the
> screen with the default of 80 columns.
> Is it reasonable trying to change the size of the hole NetHack display?
> And if so, how it is be done? With an option or do I have to apply
> a patch?

The macros COLNO and ROWNO are defined in include/global.h and I think
these define the size of a dungeon level.
The level size COULD be changed, but that would certainly have some kind
of effect on the game balance. I can't say whether having larger levels
would make the game easier or harder, but many things would certainly be
different. 

> Or is it better to keep the default window size?

Currently there is little use in tty for screen larger than the level map
plus status lines, about the only difference is that various listings
(like inventory and pick up lists) use the whole screen height. 

> I know, that the dungeon size is hard-coded, but will the dungeon size
> ever exceed the size of the default terminal?

No.

